    "status": "fail",
    "summary": "The one-line change to `apps/tempo/src/agents/issues.ts` changes the agent tool pagination offset calculation from `offset + bounded.length` to `offset + bounded.length + 1`. This introduces an off-by-one bug on pages that contain any non-final page. The spec requires clients to follow `nextOffset` until it is null, and to return at most 50 entries per page. With the +1, the caller will skip one row on the next page, and an issue or comment that happens to be at the boundary will be omitted. The condition `items.length === 50` also seems intended as a proxy for \"there may be more\", but it is not equivalent to `bounded.length < items.length` when all 50 returned items are consumed. On the last full page there is no more data, yet the tool will still emit a non-null `nextOffset`, while the database will return zero rows, causing an empty follow-up page rather than a skipped issue. In short, the change does not match the pagination semantics in the spec and breaks correctness on intermediate pages.",
    "checked": [
