        "line": 50,
        "text": "The new nextOffset computation skips one row on every paginated page.",
        "evidence": {
          "quote": "    nextOffset: bounded.length < items.length || items.length === 50 ? offset + bounded.length + 1 : null,",
          "why": "If the agent receives 60 items, the first page contains items[0..49] (bounded.length=50) and should return nextOffset=50 so the next page starts at items[50]. The code returns 101 because offset is 0 and bounded.length 50 plus 1. Even on a page where bounded.length < items.length is true, adding +1 means the next SQL OFFSET will jump past one element. This contradicts docs/09 Git Forge.md which says lists return at most 50 items and nextOffset must point to the next page to follow."
        }
      }
    ]
